---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="How to Play | Driftaku">
    <main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12 prose prose-invert">
        <h1 class="text-5xl font-black text-white uppercase tracking-tighter mb-8">How to Drift</h1>
        
        <div class="bg-slate-900 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 mb-8">
            <h2 class="text-indigo-400">The Goal</h2>
            <p>Connect the <strong>Start Anime</strong> to the <strong>Target Anime</strong> using the shortest path possible. Every connection must be supported by the database—either they share a Studio, a Voice Actor, or a Character.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-10">Game Mechanics</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
            <li><strong>Warehouse:</strong> Nodes start in the sidebar. Click to deploy them onto your workspace.</li>
            <li><strong>The Graph:</strong> Use the <em>Move Tool</em> to arrange nodes spatially.</li>
            <li><strong>Linking:</strong> Use the <em>Link Tool</em> to select two nodes. If they are officially related in our database, the edge will lock in bright purple.</li>
            <li><strong>Winning:</strong> You must create a continuous path of purple edges from the Start node to the Target node.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="bg-slate-900 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/10 mt-10">
            <h2 class="text-emerald-400">Multiplayer Tips</h2>
            <p>In "Vs. Friends" mode, you are the architect. Your goal is to make the path as <em>difficult as possible</em> for your opponent. Use <strong>Isolated Clusters</strong> (nodes that don't help the path) to confuse them!</p>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>